<title>USA: Mid-America buys Florida apartments.</title>
<headline>Mid-America buys Florida apartments.</headline>
<dateline>MEMPHIS, Tenn. 1997-06-01</dateline>
<text>
<p>Mid-America Apartment Communities Inc said  on Friday it bought a 336-unit apartment complex in Jacksonville, Fla., for $15.2 million.</p>
<p>The Oaks at Deerwood property is encumbered by a $14.7 million tax-free bond which Mid-America purchased at closing and which it plans to remarket during the next year, the company said in a news release.</p>
<p>The acquisition brings Mid-America's holdings in Jacksonville to 2,118 apartments.</p>
